// S441 reproducer — addendum-3 T7: SPEC §6.5.1 contradicts itself on whether `@arr.push(x)` updates.
// Compiler SHA: cf62b4154 (origin/main at dispatch); SPEC.md §6.5.1 ~L2527-2540
// Command: bun compiler/bin/scrml.js compile docs/changes/s441-audit-gap-filing/repro/tut-spec-6-5-1-push-reactivity.scrml --output-dir <scratch>
// SPEC text: DQ-2 paragraph — "Array mutation methods (`.push()`, `.splice()`, `.pop()`, etc.) do NOT trigger
//           reactivity on their own." … "this rewrite is NOT guaranteed in production builds". Normative rule,
//           same subsection — "it SHALL rewrite the call to: 1. Clone … 3. Write the clone back to `@name` via
//           `_scrml_reactive_set`, which triggers all subscribers." (§66.11's header note says it supersedes the
//           DQ-2 paragraph; the paragraph is still inline and unstruck.)
// Actual:   client.js `{ _scrml_cs_reactive_get("items").push(2); _scrml_cs_reactive_set("items", _scrml_cs_reactive_get("items")); }`
//           (in place, no clone — see g-cell-mutators-skip-clone-then-write-back). EXECUTED (happy-dom): the
//           paragraph shows 1, after clicking the button 2 — push DOES update.
<program>
<items> = [1]
function add() { @items.push(2) }
<button onclick=add()>add</button>
<p>${@items.length}</p>
</program>
